<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jasaw Chan K'awiil I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 682–c. 734</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jasaw Chan K'awiil I was the ruler of the Maya city of Tikal, in modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guatemala">Guatemala</a>, from 682 to about 734. In 695 he defeated Calakmul, Tikal's great rival, ending a long period of eclipse, and he commemorated the victory on carved wooden lintels. He was buried in Temple I, the great pyramid on the east side of the main plaza, which was completed after his death.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jasaw-chan-kawiil-i.jpg" alt="Jasaw Chan K'awiil I" width="320" height="482" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: A.Skromnitsky (A.Skromnitsky) · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:MutalImage3.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
